# Data conversion between gibibyte and tebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gibibyte and tebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GiB to 0.0009TiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GiB yields 0.0014TiB; backward, converting 1TiB to 1024GiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TiB yields 1536.0GiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(forward_whole->to(TiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(forward_fractional->to(TiB))
backward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(backward_whole->to(GiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(backward_fractional->to(GiB))

<<< stdout
0.0009TiB
0.0014TiB
1024GiB
1536.0GiB

<<< stderr
